## Instructions

1. **Check current local state:** Assess contents in `.agent-data/` directories in workspaces and/or `~/.agent-data/`.
2. Fetch new and updated issues, pull requests, discussions, etc. on GitHub and assess.
3. Assess related and linked issues, comments, pull requests, etc.
4. Update both local data and GitHub data so they are in sync.
5. Create a report in `~/.agent-data/` summarizing what you did (time spent, token usage, estimated cost if available).
6. Build a weekly report of usage statistics and operations performed in `~/.agent-data/weekly/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md`.
7. Do not write code; your output is purely critical feedback and suggested changes/tests. Do not commit code. Do not push code. Do not approve PRs. Do not close tickets.

Occasionally research good database applications for storing agent memory in that is better than markdown files.

### Accessing github
Feel free to use what costs less tokens and gets you the best data fastest.  You will have github's MCP server, gh cli, and github graphql access as well.   If any other tool would make things easier on your work, let me know.


